  "info.dragonrise_reforge.kv1": "",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.kv2": "The KV-2 is a Soviet heavy tank of 1940: a KV-1 chassis carrying a massive turret with a 152mm M-10 howitzer. A single HE shell can level bunkers and light armour, but the turret traverses painfully slowly, reloading takes forever, and its towering silhouette is easy to spot.",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.l1a2": "",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.lcm": "The LCM (Landing Craft, Mechanized) is the steel landing craft used by US forces in WWII to put tanks and vehicles straight onto a beach: it carries one medium tank or dozens of troops and unloads over a drop-down bow ramp. Two .50 cal machine guns suppress the shoreline, but its thin steel hull means it has to rely on speed and smoke to get ashore.",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.leopard2a4": "",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.lvt": "",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.m10booker": "",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.m1126": "M1126 Stryker ICV, the baseline 8x8 wheeled armored personnel carrier of the US Stryker Brigade Combat Teams, fitted with a remote weapon station.",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.m1128": "M1128 Mobile Gun System, the fire-support variant of the Stryker family, armed with a 105 mm M68 rifled gun for direct-fire infantry support.",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.m113": "",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.m1296": "M1296 Dragoon, the up-gunned Stryker variant with a remotely operated 30 mm XM813 cannon turret, intended to replace the M1128 MGS.",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.m1a1hc": "M1A1 Abrams Main Battle Tank, the first mass-produced improved variant of the M1 Abrams series. Equipped with an M256 120mm smoothbore gun, composite armor, and gas turbine power system, it served as the main battle tank of the US Army from the late Cold War to the early 21st century.",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.m1a2sepv1": "M1A2 SEPv1 Abrams main battle tank, the first version of the System Enhancement Package: second-generation FLIR and full-color displays, plus an upgraded digital backbone and fire-control computer for better day/night target acquisition and information sharing.",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.m1a2sepv2": "",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.m2": "",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.m270": "",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.m3a3": "",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.m3stuart": "",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.m4a2": "",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.m4a2_105": "",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.markv": "",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.maus": "",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.mi24p": "",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.mi24v": "Mi-24V Hind, an improved variant of the Soviet Mi-24 attack helicopter developed by Mil. Armed with a GSh-23L 23mm twin-barrel cannon on the right side of the nose, plus S-8 rockets, 9M114 Shturm-S anti-tank missiles, Kh-39 air-to-ground missiles and 9M336 surface-to-air missiles on the wing pylons, it was one of the most iconic attack helicopters of the Cold War.",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.mk19": "",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.motuo": "",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.mv3": "",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.mv3_armed": "MV3 Armed Tactical Truck, the weapon-carrier variant of the FAW MV3 family. A roof-mounted heavy machine gun provides self-defense and fire support while retaining the vehicle\u0027s tactical transport capability.",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.mv3_supply": "MV3 Supply Truck, the logistics variant of the FAW MV3 tactical truck family. Designed to haul ammunition, fuel and supplies to front-line units, keeping the assault force continuously provisioned.",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.nh90": "",
  "info.dragonrise_reforge.npds114": "",
